  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Merz vows to keep coalition together for Germany's 'democratic future'",
      "link": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqm27p8enwmko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "description": "The chancellor has come under increasing pressure after resounding state election defeats, but says the results \"go far beyond my own person\"",
      "source_name": "BBC World News",
      "published": "2026-09-21T16:54:56"
    },
    {
      "title": "Chancellor vows to stay on for Germany’s ‘democratic future’ after latest loss to far-right AfD",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/germany-chancellor-freidrich-merz-cdu-christian-democratic-union-state-election-defeats-mecklenburg-western-pomerania-berlin",
      "description": "<p>Merz seeks to shore up support after CDU loses two state elections and is ejected from Mecklenburg parliament</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/german-state-election-humiliation-friedrich-merz-borrowed-time-cdu-unrest-grows\">Latest German election humiliation puts Merz on borrowed time as CDU unrest grows</a></p></li></ul><p>Germany’s beleaguered leader, Friedrich Merz, has vowed to keep his fractious coalition government together for the good of the country’s “democratic future” after his conservative party suffered a drubbing at the polls in two state elections.</p><p>Merz, who has vowed to plough ahead with an unpopular reform agenda, dismissed speculation over his position, saying it was vital that he and his coalition government remained in place.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/germany-chancellor-freidrich-merz-cdu-christian-democratic-union-state-election-defeats-mecklenburg-western-pomerania-berlin\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T15:38:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "Latest German election humiliation puts Merz on borrowed time as CDU unrest grows",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/german-state-election-humiliation-friedrich-merz-borrowed-time-cdu-unrest-grows",
      "description": "<p>Chancellor acknowledges disastrous state election results but vow to push on is likely to further alienate voters, and his own party</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/germany-chancellor-freidrich-merz-cdu-christian-democratic-union-state-election-defeats-mecklenburg-western-pomerania-berlin\">German chancellor clinging to power after another loss to far-right AfD</a></p><p></p></li></ul><p>Friedrich Merz called it a “disaster”, and that was even before the full scale of the catastrophe for himself and his conservative Christian Democratic Union (CDU) came into view after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/20/friedrich-merz-chancellor-germany-state-elections-cdu-afd-linke-berlin\">Sunday’s state elections</a>.</p><p>In what one outlet called a <a href=\"https://www.zeit.de/politik/deutschland/2026-09/friedrich-merz-cdu-krise-landtagswahlen-bundeskanzler\">“power move”</a>, the German chancellor made a highly unusual televised speech just minutes after polls closed in the states of Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, attempting to get ahead of the narrative with a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/20/friedrich-merz-chancellor-germany-state-elections-cdu-afd-linke-berlin\">pledge to stay on and fight for his economic recovery programme</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/german-state-election-humiliation-friedrich-merz-borrowed-time-cdu-unrest-grows\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T10:04:46"
    }
  ]
